(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers."] [15 1 "// signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C"] [16 1 "// handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;"] [17 1 "// the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL"] [18 1 "// signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux."] [19 1 "// The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:"] [20 1 "// a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked."] [26 1 "// sysPidfdSendSignal is pidfd_send_signal's syscall number (424 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)"] [31 39 "// the main thread's wake-up from a blocking wait"] [32 39 "// any arrival (sigwait)"] [33 39 "// tripped, its handler to run"] [34 39 "// is_tripped"] [35 39 "// pthread_sigmask's mask"] [36 39 "// arrived while blocked (sigpending)"] [37 39 "// notified on sigCh"] [38 39 "// arrivals so far (pidfd_send_signal's wait)"] [39 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's fd, -1 none"] [41 2 "// sigHandlers are the Python-level handlers (Handlers[n].func), touched under the GIL"] [43 21 "// default_int_handler"] [48 1 "// startSignals starts the receiver once."] [61 1 "// ownSignalHook, when set, handles a signal pyi sends itself (killSignal of its own pid, raise_signal) before the"] [62 1 "// signal module does (queue 220: faulthandler's handlers, and the default action that ends the process): handled true"] [63 1 "// and the call returns."] [66 1 "// signalTakenHook, when set, says a signal's handler is another module's (queue 220: faulthandler.register without"] [67 1 "// chain replaces the Python handler, as its sigaction does): the Python handler is not tripped."] [70 1 "// deliverSignal is the C handler: held when blocked, else tripped; the wakeup fd written."] [90 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [102 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [103 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [134 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [135 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [162 1 "// exitSigint is Modules/main.c's exit_sigint after an unhandled KeyboardInterrupt (queue 231): SIGINT's default action"] [163 1 "// restored and the signal sent to the process, so that its parent sees it killed by SIGINT; else exit status 130."] [169 38 "// delivered to this thread on the call's return; another one's at the latest here"] [174 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [175 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [176 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [188 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [189 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [199 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [213 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [232 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [233 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [253 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [254 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [299 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [421 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [444 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [553 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [557 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [610 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [681 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [682 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[53 35] [85 26] [112 12] [112 22] [125 60] [155 22] [179 40] [193 50] [301 14] [301 24] [338 31] [353 14] [353 24] [355 39] [380 40] [402 26] [416 40] [427 63] [463 37] [480 32] [495 31] [537 37] [586 14] [586 24] [615 40] [646 40] [669 35] [677 104] [684 16] [684 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


